---
/**
 * Fender Jazzmaster dating guide. THIRD OF THE MODEL-AXIS SPOKES.
 *
 * Sibling of fender-stratocaster-dating-guide.astro and
 * fender-telecaster-dating-guide.astro. Built on joe/jazzmaster-dating-spoke,
 * stacked on joe/tele-dating-spoke, because every model page edits the hub's
 * "Go Deeper" chips and the sitemap list and would otherwise conflict. Joe is
 * holding the whole model set to go live at once.
 *
 * WHAT MAKES THE JAZZMASTER PAGE DIFFERENT. Do not clone the Strat or Tele
 * structure; this model's story is its own:
 *   - The PICKGUARD is the spine of the page (Joe asked for all types called
 *     out, gold included). Four combinations across three materials, and the
 *     screw count changes with them: 9 screws on the gold anodized guard,
 *     13 from mid-1959 on. Custom colors got WHITE, not tortoiseshell.
 *   - It was the FIRST Fender production guitar with a rosewood fingerboard
 *     (1958, a year ahead of the Tele and Strat), and also the first to move
 *     OFF the slab board (spring 1962, ahead of the Strat's August).
 *   - Three inlay eras, not two: clay, then pearloid, then BLOCK inlays on a
 *     bound board from mid-1966. Neither the Strat nor the Tele page has that.
 *   - The dual-circuit electronics, the floating bridge and separate floating
 *     tremolo with its trem-lock button, and the witch hat knobs are all
 *     Jazzmaster-specific.
 *   - Foam rot under the pickups is a condition issue unique to this model.
 *
 * JOE'S REVIEW RULES, carried over from the Strat and Tele pages:
 *   - Features give a WINDOW, often a wider one than the serial. They
 *     corroborate the serial rather than beating it. Only the neck heel date
 *     and the body date give a month.
 *   - The serial belongs in the second pass, read as one vote among several.
 *   - Never call a feature "model-specific" without checking it.
 *   - Never say "bare wood" about a body date. Say the date is written
 *     directly on the body.
 *   - Keep a photo caption on the one thing the photo is for.
 *   - Open the photo before repeating any color or layout claim about it.
 *
 * LOGO COLOR: GOLD. Joe ruled 2026-08-10 that the Jazzmaster spaghetti logo is
 * GOLD, the same as the Stratocaster, and the evolution guide's silver/chrome
 * wording was corrected in the same pass. Do NOT put silver back on this model.
 * The cluster now reads: Stratocaster gold, Jazzmaster gold, and the Telecaster
 * alone splits silver on the standard model from gold on the Custom, which the
 * 1959 Telecaster guide states directly. That Telecaster split is deliberate.
 *
 * The knock-on, same as on the Strat page: because the spaghetti AND the
 * transition logos are both gold here, COLOR CANNOT SEPARATE THEM. The tell is
 * the WEIGHT of the script, thin and delicate versus noticeably heavier. Never
 * write the change as silver-to-gold on this model.
 *
 * SOURCE ERROR, now FIXED at the source (2026-08-10, Joe's go-ahead): the
 * evolution guide's "Standard Finish" section used to say "The sunburst always
 * received a white pickguard", contradicting its own pickguard summary table
 * (sunburst = tortoiseshell, custom colors = white celluloid) and its
 * custom-color section. The table was right and the sentence has been corrected
 * on the live guide, so the guide and this page now agree. If a future edit
 * reintroduces "sunburst = white guard" anywhere, it is the error coming back.
 *
 * Content facts trace to Joe's own live pages and VG_FACTS.md: VG-0053,
 * VG-0056 / VG-0057 (pickup dating and era), VG-0066 to VG-0068 (serial eras,
 * ranges NOT asserted), VG-0070 (the slab and veneer rosewood context),
 * VG-0071 (CBS-era tells including bound boards with block inlays circa 1966),
 * VG-0072 (pre-CBS definition), VG-0073 / VG-0074 (custom color and refinish
 * value). Primary on-site source is the Jazzmaster evolution guide, plus
 * fender-physical-features.astro, fender-pot-codes.astro (1 Meg from the
 * Jazzmaster's debut), fender-pickup-dates.astro (Jazzmaster poles were never
 * staggered at the factory) and fender-neck-dates.astro.
 *
 * NOT YET IN VG_FACTS, flagged for a joes-vintage-databases PR: the gold
 * anodized guard window and its 9-screw count; the 13-screw change; the
 * custom-color white-guard rule; the spring-1962 slab-to-veneer date being
 * ahead of the Stratocaster; the amber-to-white switch tip change; the witch
 * hat knob date; and the Pat. Pend. to full-patent tremolo marking.
 *
 * NO YEAR-TO-SERIAL-NUMBER TABLE, same as the sibling pages. The charts live
 * once, on the hub.
 */
