  ],
  [
    "1962",
    "In the spring the slab rosewood board gives way to the thin curved veneer, and the Jazzmaster gets there several months before the Stratocaster does. From the middle of the year the neck heel changes from a penciled date to a rubber-stamped code that opens with the model number.",
    "Rosewood depth at the nut, plus a stamp rather than pencil handwriting on the heel.",
  ],
  [
    "1963",
    "No headline change. A 1963 carries the same specification as a late 1962, so this is a year to date from the neck stamp and the pots.",
