  ],
  [
    "1964",
    "Four changes land within months of each other, which makes this the busiest year on the model. Around the middle of the year the spaghetti logo gives way to the heavier gold transition logo. Late in the year the clay dots give way to pearloid, and the celluloid tortoiseshell guard gives way to a more stable plastic one. The Kluson stamp goes from one line to two, the coil wire changes from Formvar to plain enamel, and the pickup bottoms begin moving from black to grey.",
    "Bright dots and a heavier gold logo. If you see one you should see the other.",
  ],
  [
    "1965",
    "CBS completes the purchase in January and the guitar changes in stages. Around the middle of the year the Stratocaster-style dome knobs give way to witch hat knobs, which is the clearest single CBS marker on the instrument. Late in the year the fingerboard gains white binding and the Kluson tuners give way to Fender's own F tuners. The big-F neck plate arrives around the third quarter.",
